namespace gismo {

\page Modules Modules


/** \defgroup Modules The G+Smo modules
  *
  * G+Smo is split into different modules. Every module lives in
  * <tt>src/&lt;module&gt;/</tt> and is declared in its own
  * <tt>CMakeLists.txt</tt> with
  *
  * \code{.cmake}
  * gismo_add_module(gsNurbs DEPENDS gsCore gsDomain gsTensor gsContainers gsIO gsUtils gsMatrix)
  * \endcode
  *
  * (see <tt>cmake/gsModule.cmake</tt>). The declared dependencies form a
  * directed acyclic graph that is checked at configure time and by the
  * include checker <tt>.github/scripts/check_includes.py</tt>: the public
  * headers of a module may only include modules it depends on. The
  * modules are compiled into the single library <tt>libgismo</tt>.
  *
  * Projects that use G+Smo through CMake can ask for the modules they
  * need and link the component targets <tt>gismo::&lt;module&gt;</tt>
  * (or <tt>gismo::gismo</tt> for the whole library):
  *
  * \code{.cmake}
  * find_package(gismo REQUIRED COMPONENTS gsNurbs gsIO)
  * target_link_libraries(myapp gismo::gsNurbs gismo::gsIO)
  * \endcode
  *
  * A component target links the library and carries the include
  * directories and the components of its declared dependencies, so a
  * project keeps working unchanged when the modules become separate
  * libraries.
  *
  **/

}


